## Step 6 — Buyer Spec Audit

### Phase 1 — Top 2 RFQ Specs

Provided buyer specs: Construction Type (Prefabricated / New Construction), Roof Type (Gable / Hip / Mansard / Gambrel / Flat)

**Construction Type:** 2 values — Prefabricated vs New Construction. This is a broad intent filter. Within this MCAT (Steel Buildings), all products are prefabricated/steel-framed by definition. "New Construction" is a generic intent tag, not a steel building configurator. Marginally useful for routing but low differentiation within this MCAT. **Rank 1** (by default — it is the more useful of the two for seller routing).

**Roof Type:** 5 values — Gable / Hip / Mansard / Gambrel / Flat. Roof form is a real structural differentiator in PEB. Gable is the dominant industrial form; flat roofs are used in commercial/multi-storey; hip roofs are used in residential/institutional. This helps sellers identify the structural system required. **Rank 2.**

**Thumbnail eligibility:**
- Construction Type (Prefabricated / New Construction): These are intent/method tags, not visually distinct product forms. A prefabricated steel building and a new construction steel building look identical in a thumbnail. **Not thumbnail eligible.**
- Roof Type (Gable / Hip / Mansard / Gambrel / Flat): Each roof form has a distinct visual silhouette. Gable = triangular ridge; Hip = sloped on all four sides; Flat = horizontal roofline; Mansard = double-pitched; Gambrel = barn-style. **Thumbnail eligible.** Options: ["Gable", "Hip", "Mansard", "Gambrel", "Flat"]

